.TH AVR\-VM\-BOOTSTRAP 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-bootstrap \- Set up a RUNNING VM with your dev essentials over SSH.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm bootstrap
[OPTIONS] VM_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set up a RUNNING VM with your dev essentials over SSH.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Each selected step runs on the VM and streams its output; bootstrap stops at
the first failure. Secrets (GitHub token, forwarded env values, agent API
keys) ride SSH stdin, never argv. Disks are ephemeral, so re-run bootstrap
after every `avr vm start`. Example:
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
avr vm bootstrap cvm-abc123 --setup-github --install claude,codex \e
  --repo https://github.com/me/project --env AWS_REGION=eu-north-1
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-setup\-github\fR / \fB\-\-no\-setup\-github\fR
Forward your local `gh auth token` into the VM (gh auth login --with-token + gh auth setup-git).
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR \fITEXT\fR
Install an agent CLI (repeatable or comma-separated): claude, codex. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-forward\-agent\-creds\fR
Also forward the installed agents' API keys (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY) from your environment.
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-avr\fR
Install the avr CLI in the VM (pipx, else pip).
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Clone this git repo into the VM's home directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fITEXT\fR
Branch to check out after cloning (requires --repo). Tags, PR refs, and raw SHAs are unsupported.
.TP
\fB\-\-dotfiles\fR \fITEXT\fR
Clone this dotfiles repo and run its installer.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fITEXT\fR
Set an env var in the VM: KEY=VALUE, or a bare KEY to forward it from your environment. Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR \fITEXT\fR
Run a custom script last: an inline script, or @path to a file.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ordered plan (secrets redacted) without running.
